      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1734111384,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This is a workaround for HTTP/2 only that works because it has a flag that indicates the last fragment. To fix other protocols, TLS needs to avoid incrementing the protocol layer number when a fragment doesn't add anything to the tree on the first pass (in those cases TLS doesn't get called on subsequent passes). A similar fix was done for TCP previously.",
